Everything else matches: 9,631 − 1,152 = 8,479 rows, 68 columns, and the output path. The validation report's "sum of weights ✓" only compared the sum with what the job wrote. It never compared it with the target.

{"works": false, "confidence": 0.9, "reason": "Weights sum to 9,184,030 instead of the D2 target population of 8,002,715, so recalibration was wrong although dedupe, schema and path are fine."}

Rows: 37,675 − 777 = 36,898 ✓. The weight sum is 1,746,088, which matches the target ✓. There are 51 columns ✓. respondent_id is unique ✓. The weight mean is 1,746,088 / 36,898 ≈ 47.3 ✓, and there are no null weights. The path is correct.

The one thing I can't check from the statistics is whether the income code -9 was left unchanged. Nothing in the output suggests it was altered.

{"works": true, "confidence": 0.9, "reason": "Row count (37,675−777), weight sum (1,746,088 target), column count (51), and unique IDs all match runbook expectations."}

